    "verdict": "NARROWING. The bar-even (λ↔λᵀ) admissibility constraint rules the row-count content channels INADMISSIBLE independently of their numerical refutation: C1_sl2_schur_weyl, C2_sl3_schur_weyl, C3_sl2_qdim, C4_sl2_indicator all break P_λ = P_{λᵀ} (the `rows(λ) ≤ k` selector is not transpose-invariant — rows(λᵀ) = columns(λ)). The flat substrate weight w_λ = y_λ·χ^λ(β_D) is carrying a substantial bar-odd component (fraction 50.00%); a bar-even P_λ annihilates it, so any deviation living in the bar-odd sector is structurally unreachable. Conclusion: GAP-A-3 P_λ must be a TRANSPOSE-INVARIANT functional (e.g. of {λ,λᵀ}-symmetric statistics: n(λ)+n(λᵀ), symmetric hook/content combinations), NOT a row-count or column-count selector. This is a formalize-first refutation of the content-channel family and a constraint on the admissible family — not a new fitted P_λ (no 7th ansatz)."
